invariant: INV-13
file: tls.c
catches: unit_ca
reason: ch_connect answers a CA build's ticket that the stored epoch
  retired with CH_EAUTH again, while ch_record_init and ch_quic_init
  answer it with CH_EINVAL. The refusal comes before a byte is sent, so
  every client entry owes CH_EINVAL for it. bin/unit_ca requires that
  code for a ticket one step below the stored epoch.

--- old
        t->epoch_status = CH_EPOCH_REVOKED;
        return CH_EINVAL;
--- new
        t->epoch_status = CH_EPOCH_REVOKED;
        return CH_EAUTH;
